# Local certificate authority. NEVER commit this.
#
# The bridge generates a CA per install and keeps its private key on disk. A key
# that reached a public repository would let anyone sign a certificate for any
# domain and present it to every phone that had trusted that build — and it
# could not be undone afterwards, because the key would already be out.
#
# `--tls-dir` defaults to a real config directory so this cannot happen by
# accident. This is the belt to that pair of braces, for anyone who points it at
# a checkout on purpose.
tls/
**/ca-private-key.pem
**/ca-cert.pem
